1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,411
How many r's are in strawberry? Three. Why can a language model stumble on that? Start with the ruler it uses.

2
00:00:05,411 --> 00:00:11,319
Models process tokens, not a separate position for every letter. Counting becomes less direct, not impossible.

3
00:00:11,319 --> 00:00:14,640
Let's inspect two real tokenizers and check the count.

4
00:00:14,917 --> 00:00:20,878
A tokenizer converts text into integer IDs. A token can cover a word, part of a word, or other text.

5
00:00:20,878 --> 00:00:26,158
We ran tik token locally with both encodings shown here: lowercase inputs, no leading spaces.

6
00:00:26,158 --> 00:00:30,197
These are OpenAI encodings, not measurements of Claude's tokenizer.

7
00:00:30,458 --> 00:00:35,983
First, strawberry in c l one hundred k base: str, aw, berry. These are the exact measured IDs.

8
00:00:35,983 --> 00:00:39,621
Count r inside each chunk: one, zero, two. Add them: three.

9
00:00:39,621 --> 00:00:44,669
Three tokens matching three r's is a coincidence. Token count is not a letter-counting rule.

10
00:00:44,917 --> 00:00:50,609
Switch encodings. Strawberry now splits into st, raw, berry. Different boundaries and IDs; same spelling.

11
00:00:50,609 --> 00:00:56,238
The r counts become zero, one, two. Still three. The first r moved into another chunk, not out of the text.

12
00:00:56,238 --> 00:00:58,831
Token boundaries depend on the encoding.

13
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:05,283
Banana is one token in both encodings. Different IDs, but still three a's. One token does not mean one letter.

14
00:01:05,283 --> 00:01:10,428
Occurrence splits into occ and urrence. Both r's are in the second chunk. These IDs are also measured.

15
00:01:10,428 --> 00:01:13,936
Counting chunks and counting characters are different operations.

16
00:01:14,208 --> 00:01:21,441
Embedding lookup selects a learned vector for each token ID. These colored vectors are constructed illustrations, not real model weights.

17
00:01:21,441 --> 00:01:28,074
Ten character positions become three token positions for strawberry. Internal letters have no separate input token position.

18
00:01:28,074 --> 00:01:32,989
But vectors can carry spelling-related information. Lookup does not prove spelling was erased.

19
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:38,321
Tokenization is reversible. Decode these IDs and every letter of strawberry comes back.

20
00:01:38,321 --> 00:01:45,376
All six word-and-encoding pairs passed our Python round-trip checks. Counts across decoded fragments also matched the original strings.

21
00:01:45,376 --> 00:01:48,360
Less direct access does not mean lost characters.

22
00:01:48,625 --> 00:01:53,084
Predicting an answer is not automatically the same as running a character-counting loop.

23
00:01:53,084 --> 00:02:00,503
We tested tokenizers, not model responses. This experiment gives no model failure rate and cannot diagnose a particular wrong answer.

24
00:02:00,503 --> 00:02:03,265
Keep the conclusion as narrow as the evidence.

25
00:02:03,542 --> 00:02:09,307
Run Python's count operation. Strawberry has three r's; banana has three a's; occurrence has two r's.

26
00:02:09,307 --> 00:02:15,590
These results were executed locally. This code view reconstructs recorded output; it is not a live screen capture.

27
00:02:15,590 --> 00:02:19,782
Run the operation. Inspect the result. Fluency alone verifies nothing.

28
00:02:20,042 --> 00:02:27,573
Tokens do not make models unable to count. A model may answer correctly, use a scratchpad, use character-level representations, or call tools.

29
00:02:27,573 --> 00:02:32,867
Scratchpads still do not guarantee correctness. Two encodings do not establish how every model works.

30
00:02:32,867 --> 00:02:38,181
Our claim: token positions differ from character positions. Not a universal failure diagnosis.

31
00:02:38,458 --> 00:02:43,096
Try another word: encode it, inspect the IDs, decode it, then count the target letter.

32
00:02:43,096 --> 00:02:47,072
A token is a processing unit, not a spelling unit. Use the right ruler.

33
00:02:47,072 --> 00:02:49,746
Strawberry: three r's. Verified locally.
